 "equipment_type": "Room controller (fan coil, radiator, VAV)",
 "applies_to": "Regin Regio Midi pre-programmed room controllers with display, which are the Midi models that can talk BACnet MS/TP.",
 "summary": "Regio Midi is a wall-mounted room controller for heating, cooling, change-over, fan coil and VAV applications. The RS485 port runs EXOline, Modbus or BACnet MS/TP; BACnet is only offered on the display models and is switched on from the parameter menu or Application tool. All Midi models share one fixed object list, so objects for hardware a model lacks (CO2, fan, VAV, extra zone) simply stay unused.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "1.7 or later (AV 35, AV 36 and AV 42 need 1.7-1-04 or newer)",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Object list from Appendix C of the Regio Midi manual (rev F), pages 107-111. Older firmware (1.6 and earlier) uses a different list; Regin points to the 1.6 variable list for those.",
  "The manual prints 16 placeholder objects named AV02, AV18-AV21, AV24, AV25, AV32-AV34, BI06, BV03-BV06 and MSV6 as 'Not used'; they are left out here.",
  "Value objects are not commandable (no priority array); a write simply sets the value.",
  "AV 38 (CO2 high alarm limit) is printed with unit °C in the manual; it is a CO2 level, shown here as ppm.",
  "The 0/1/2 state numbering on MV 7-9 is as printed; the other multistate objects start at 1."
 ],
